<section class="formula">
    <h2>Mulch Formulas & Conversion Standards</h2>
    <p>Landscape calculations convert surface area square footage and layer depth inches into cubic yards or bag counts:</p>
    
    <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; margin: 1.5rem 0;">
        <div style="background: var(--input-bg); padding: 1.25rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border);">
            <h3 style="margin-top: 0; font-size: 1.1rem; color: #2563eb;">Cubic Yards Formula</h3>
            <p style="font-size: 0.9rem;">Area in square feet multiplied by depth in feet divided by 27:</p>
            <p><code>Cubic Yards = (Square Feet x (Depth / 12)) / 27</code></p>
        </div>

        <div style="background: var(--input-bg); padding: 1.25rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border);">
            <h3 style="margin-top: 0; font-size: 1.1rem; color: #7c3aed;">Mulch Bag Conversion</h3>
            <p style="font-size: 0.9rem;">One cubic yard contains 27 cubic feet. That equals 13.5 two-cubic-foot bags:</p>
            <p><code>Bags = Cubic Feet / Bag Size (cu ft)</code></p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

