<section class="faq">
    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

    <h3>How many bags of mulch equal one cubic yard?</h3>
    <p>One cubic yard equals 27 cubic feet. If you buy standard 2.0 cubic foot bags, you need 13.5 bags (14 full bags) to equal one cubic yard of bulk mulch.</p>

    <h3>How deep should mulch be laid in flower beds?</h3>
    <p>A depth of 3 inches is optimal for suppressing weeds and conserving moisture. Laying mulch deeper than 4 inches can smother plant root systems and block water penetration.</p>

    <h3>When is buying bulk mulch cheaper than buying bagged mulch?</h3>
    <p>Buying bulk mulch delivered by dump truck is generally more cost efficient when your project requires more than 2 to 3 cubic yards (27 to 40 bags). For small garden beds, bagged mulch offers easier transport.</p>

    <h3>Does wood mulch settle over time?</h3>
    <p>Yes. Organic wood mulch compresses and decomposes by approximately 15 to 20 percent over the first season. Adding a light 1-inch topdressing layer each spring maintains proper soil protection.</p>
